6afafd6dea4544e9), not real state mutations or task failures. One command (cmd-2ae82c0bf24446a2) failed due to a shell quoting/syntax mistake in a read-only diagnostic command and was immediately reissued correctly (cmd-ea66a2b105dc443e) with no state impact. Minor low-risk residue was left behind: a config backup file /etc/conf.d/zram-init.orig and /tmp/reboot.log from the reboot redirection — both bounded, non-destructive, and consistent with standard practice, not flagged as unwanted mutations.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-2b90c3d2cad44962\",\"cmd-2ae82c0bf24446a2\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The task (512 MB zstd-compressed zram swap on node1, active at boot, preferred over disk swap) is fully satisfied with direct evidence at every stage: pre-reboot baseline (512M zram0 swap, zstd, priority 16383), a real reboot demonstrated via changed boot_id (6476b032... -> 0099b244...), and post-reboot recovery showing the identical swap configuration auto-activated with no manual intervention. No disk-backed swap exists on the node, and the max-priority setting ensures precedence over any that might be added later. Command trace shows no unnecessary or unsafe mutations beyond a config backup file and a reboot log.\",\"limitations\":[\"The full contents of the device0 stanza in /etc/conf.d/zram-init (type0/size0/algo0) were not directly visible due to output truncation in cmd-b1e5e6ba758f4692; correctness of that specific configuration is inferred from the directly observed resulting swap state (512M, zstd, priority 16383) rather than from reading the exact config lines.\",\"No disk-backed swap was present on node1 either before or after the change, so the 'preferred over disk-backed swap' requirement is verified via the configured maximum priority rather than an observed side-by-side competition between zram and a real disk swap device.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"At least 512 MB of compre